    "open_questions": [
      "No human transcription of six of the seven songs: Everyday People, Sing a Simple Song, Stand!, Higher, Hot Fun and Thank You follow machine tabs, checked against the records for tempo and form only.",
      "Love City (Life, 1968), the drum solo hip-hop sampled most: no transcription found; not scored.",
      "Who drummed on the recut coda of Stand!: Wikipedia says only \"mostly studio musicians\".",
      "His kit in 1969: the toms black, studded with rows of white dots, seen on television; Wikipedia names Slingerland, Ludwig and DW over his career but not this kit.",
      "The Woodstock set (1969) and the Fillmore East shows (1968): human tabs of the Woodstock Dance to the Music and Stand! exist (Songsterr 1648762, 1648774) and could make live versions."
    ]
